## Why This Is Asked

Tests at the beginner level often miss realistic offline scenarios and deterministic retries. This question probes practical E2E thinking: isolation, network control, and idempotent submission.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end orchestration of multi-step flows
- Auto-save timing and state persistence (e.g., localStorage/IndexedDB)
- Offline/online transition handling and reconciling state
- Mocking external APIs (identity) for determinism
- Ensuring single, idempotent final submit

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright sketch (context-level offline, data isolation, mocked API)
const context = await browser.newContext({ storageState: 'test-user.json' });
const page = await context.newPage();
await context.setOffline(true);
await page.goto('https://finapp/onboarding');
// perform step interactions, wait for auto-save marker, then go online
await context.setOffline(false);
// verify single submit
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to mobile vs desktop layouts?
- How would you validate that auto-save writes to the correct storage (localStorage vs IndexedDB) across browsers?

